Level 3: Challenge
The book’s rule of thumb: above 6% pay it off, 4% to 6% do both, below 4% invest. Write book_rule(loan_rate) that returns “Pay off”, “Do both”, or “Invest”, and apply it to loans at 3%, 5%, and 7%.

ExcelPythonR


With rates in A2:A4, write the rule in B2 and fill down.






NoteSolution





=IF(A2 &gt; 6%, "Pay off", IF(A2 &gt;= 4%, "Do both", "Invest"))






#| exercise: payoff_3_py
def book_rule(loan_rate):
    # your code here
    pass

[book_rule(r) for r in [0.03, 0.05, 0.07]]


Use if loan_rate &gt; 0.06:, then elif loan_rate &gt;= 0.04:, then the rest.


Solution. 
def book_rule(loan_rate):
    if loan_rate &gt; 0.06:
        return "Pay off"
    elif loan_rate &gt;= 0.04:
        return "Do both"
    return "Invest"

[book_rule(r) for r in [0.03, 0.05, 0.07]]


